1
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,580
An afternoon after the rain,
as if she were calling out to me

2
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
I walked while looking back,
holding Gar-chan's hand

3
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:42,460
That mysterious feeling I had back then

4
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:47,680
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

5
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones

6
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:01,600
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

7
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,060
the arrogant-faced politicians
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties too

8
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:14,720
Go on, turn that corner over there

9
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone

10
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,620
Over there is Kameariii

11
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:28,000
Well, surely it's Kameariii

12
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:33,040
Everyone, come on over to our town

13
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:34,640
Thank you

14
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:39,800
Ryo-san, top-class human being

15
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:54,980
I'm starving.

16
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:00,860
Listening to Senpai's stomach growl,

17
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:03,180
I'm getting hungry too.

18
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:03,840
Yeah.

19
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,340
I'm about to die of hunger.

20
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,500
Stop whining.

21
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,000
You're not special.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,060
Everyone here hasn't eaten anything since last night,
you know.

23
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,160
It's a health checkup, after all.

24
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,400
Why can't we eat before a health checkup?

25
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:22,240
There are various reasons for the tests.

26
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,320
Just bear with it a little.

27
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:26,060
Once the tests are over,
you can eat your fill.

28
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:30,300
Then let's all go out and
get something good for dinner.

29
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:31,300
Let's do that.

30
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,820
We'll treat you.

31
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,160
How about all-you-can-eat yakiniku?

32
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,060
Yakiniku!

33
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:41,140
Chief

34
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,740
Let's go, let's go

35
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,200
All-you-can-drink barium

36
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,980
You idiot,
all-you-can-drink barium is no treat at all!

37
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,820
Then let's take X-rays together.

38
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,200
Like this, like this.

39
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,640
It's not a photo booth sticker, you know!

40
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,760
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

41
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:59,340
Anyway, let's hurry and get it over with in a flash,
in a flash.

42
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,980
Are you really okay
being this happy, Ryotsu?

43
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,820
What if they find something
abnormal in the checkup?

44
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:10,080
Not me,
there's absolutely no way that would happen.

45
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:13,800
Look, look at this body,
it's the very picture of health!

46
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:18,400
Illness progresses out of sight, you know.

47
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:23,160
People who overestimate their own
bodies like that are the most dangerous.

48
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:27,380
In your case,
your diet's a complete mess, senpai.

49
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,200
For lunch it's always ramen,
katsudon, and curry rice.

50
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,520
When money runs out, you make do
with nothing but furikake for a week.

51
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,240
Or you eat the grass
growing by the roadside.

52
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,700
It's as if you've never given
nutritional balance a single thought.

53
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:43,360
You might turn into a department
store of adult diseases.

54
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,080
Look it up and you'll see.

55
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,520
Right, then, Ryotsu.

56
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:50,160
If the checkup turns up even
the slightest abnormality...

57
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:52,000
there's no all-you-can-eat yakiniku.

58
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,440
Aw, that's not fair, Chief!

59
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,140
Why is it only me?

60
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,300
Then the Chief's in it too, you know.

61
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,360
Everyone's in this together, got it?

62
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,120
If anything turns up in the checkup...

63
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,080
that one won't be getting any yakiniku,
mind you.

64
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:04,640
Understood?

65
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,660
Somehow I'm starting to get worried.

66
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:26,080
My heart's been pounding a bit lately,

67
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:28,320
and my blood pressure's a little high too.

68
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:31,600
I get stomach aches sometimes too.

69
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,320
Maybe it's already too late for all of us.

70
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:38,580
See, my heart's pounding again.

71
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:43,380
A man like Terai,
who lived a steady, by-the-book life,

72
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:45,860
No way.

73
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:49,200
Hey, don't say such stupid things.

74
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:53,920
and a hot-tempered type like the Chief
could suddenly become a goner one day.

75
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:55,360
Don't scare us like that.

76
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,120
That's right, senior.

77
00:04:57,120 --> 00:05:01,180
Nakagawa, you're always going
on about gourmet food, too.

78
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,860
That kind of diet is
the most dangerous of all.

79
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:07,820
Some terrible disease could be
progressing without you noticing.

80
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:11,140
Come to think of it,
haven't you lost a bit of weight lately?

81
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,660
That's not true at all.

82
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,680
You look pale.

83
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,880
The Chief hasn't had much appetite
since the other day, either.

84
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,420
Looks like I'm the only healthy one here.

85
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:27,120
My body's built differently
from those weak modern people.

86
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,400
There's not a single thing wrong with me.

87
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,300
Except for my head.

88
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,480
My head's as sturdy as can be, too.

89
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,620
The other day,
I was drunk and riding a bicycle,

90
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:38,020
and I smashed right through a
concrete block wall with my head.

91
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,920
You idiot!

92
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,440
I'm talking about what's inside, you fool.

93
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,860
And you shouldn't be riding a
bicycle drunk in the first place!

94
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,960
Please, everyone, keep it down.

95
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,320
I'm terribly sorry.

96
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:53,580
Please be careful.

97
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:59,520
Chief, you can't do that!
Shouting in a hospital like that!

98
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:00,880
You're a real piece of work, you know that?

99
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:01,520
There you go again.

100
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,580
My pulse feels like it's
racing abnormally fast.

101
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:09,520
My stomach's acting up too,
and my chest is pounding again.

102
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:14,240
Looks like I'm the only one who
gets to eat yakiniku after all.

103
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,560
Alright, the health checkup is ready for you now,
please go ahead.

104
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,180
Yes.

105
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:19,720
Right

106
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,180
Left

107
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:22,460
Down

108
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,300
Zero intersections on both sides.

109
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,820
Wow, amazing,
it keeps going up and up, Chief!

110
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:34,380
Chief, calm down, calm down!

111
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:37,540
What's going to happen to the house
loan if something happens to you?

112
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:41,780
Am I going to be all right? Doctor! Doctor!

113
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,640
What is this white lump?

114
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:46,900
Doctor!

115
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,620
Don't worry. He's dead. Dead.

116
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,440
The m-monitor!

117
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,260
I just blew into it like they told me.

118
00:06:58,540 --> 00:06:59,840
I-it's not humanly possible!

119
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,620
I'm bad at this, drinking this stuff.

120
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,500
Nobody's good at drinking barium, you know.

121
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:08,480
No, I think there was one right around me.

122
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:12,980
Seconds.

123
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,600
Seconds.

124
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,900
Is it that good?

125
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:19,340
When you're hungry, everything tastes good.

126
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,980
No wonder he eats weeds off the roadside.

127
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:24,620
He really eats weeds?

128
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,020
No, that's not all.

129
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:31,480
When he's hungry, he catches flying
bugs with his bare hands and eats them.

130
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:35,000
He said that if he tried, there's
nothing in this world he couldn't eat.

131
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,640
Come to think of it,
I once saw him eating Ushikan's shoe.

132
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:45,260
Yeah, that guy would do it. I've seen
him clinging to something at the park too.

133
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,600
It's not gross, it's just painful,
the stuff you're saying, you idiot.

134
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:51,680
Okay, moving on.

135
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:14,520
Health checkup this way, please.

136
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:23,200
Yeah Where did Senpai go? Forget him,
we're healthier without that guy around.

137
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,180
Whoa.

138
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:25,680
Eyes.

139
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:33,740
I always...

140
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:33,960
Let's see.

141
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,800
This one too?

142
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,740
All three of you let yourselves
get this bad before coming in!

143
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:48,200
Doctor, what's wrong with us?

144
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,920
Is it really that bad?

145
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:52,180
Since we're here, please tell us straight.

146
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:55,320
No, I'm not mentally prepared yet.

147
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:58,240
No, you should really
listen properly, Terai.

148
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:01,920
Wait, Nakagawa, even I would be
shaken if someone said it so bluntly.

149
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:02,880
Right, right.

150
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:07,500
No, let's proceed carefully
and examine this in more detail.

151
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,680
Y-yes!

152
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:17,740
S-sensei, what on earth is this...

153
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:20,140
No, it's dangerous if he thrashes about.

154
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,640
What's going to happen to us now?

155
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,200
Well, that is...

156
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,340
Looks like that's how it's gonna be

157
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:36,540
Here we go!

158
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,980
You really made me look
like a complete fool earlier!

159
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:41,060
You lot are gonna get humiliated too!

160
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:58,000
What was that just now?

161
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:04,820
Aaaaaah!

162
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:14,220
Ugh, Ryotsu! Do you know where you are?

163
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:20,720
I'm terribly sorry. What are grown
adults talking about inside a hospital?

164
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,200
I'm terribly sorry.

165
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,840
Unbelievable. Professor, what happened?

166
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:31,200
Well, this is the X-ray of
a man named Ryotsu Kankichi.

167
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,260
This is a tremendous discovery.

168
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:36,440
Look, this is the skull of modern man.

169
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,960
This is a chimpanzee's skull.

170
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,760
And this is Ryotsu's skull.

171
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,640
It's like watching the process of evolution.

172
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:48,380
If anything, it's closer to an early human.

173
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:50,540
From the front and below,
it looks just like a chimpanzee's.

174
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:54,640
So I created a three-dimensional model
of the skull from three-view drawings.

175
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:58,780
This is scary.

176
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,280
It looks like Peking Man!

177
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,460
Java Man, is it?

178
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:05,120
No, he's European-type
from over 500,000 years ago.

179
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:05,780
Cro-Magnon.

180
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,540
No, Neanderthal, maybe?

181
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,440
Neanderthals evolved much further than that.

182
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,280
He's a living fossil.

183
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,800
We have to investigate this man thoroughly.

184
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:17,940
Is everyone done?

185
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:20,080
Well, now we just wait for the results.

186
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,160
Well, I'm sure I'm fine.

187
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:24,760
Come on, yakiniku, yakiniku!

188
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:27,120
Where are the three of them?

189
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,320
No, they're worried about their results.

190
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,900
I just hope I don't have to get a retest.

191
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,420
You, Ruth Kankitsu-san

192
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:36,240
Yeah, that's right.

193
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:38,640
There are still more tests left.

194
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:43,500
Aaaaaaah!

195
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,200
Aaaaaaah!

196
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,360
Aaaaaaah!

197
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:46,920
Aaaaaaah!

198
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:47,840
Aaaaaaah!

199
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:48,160
Aaaaaaah!

200
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:50,080
Aaaaaaah!

201
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,400
Eeeeeeeh!

202
00:11:55,980 --> 00:12:02,720
Eeeeeeeh!

203
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,740
This is

204
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:16,020
Awake, are you? Ryotsu Kankichi-kun.

205
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:18,320
W-what is this?

206
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:25,960
Welcome, Ryotsu-kun, to our laboratory.

207
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:29,500
I am Serizawa,
director of this research institute.

208
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,620
This is a research laboratory!

209
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:35,920
What is going on?

210
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:39,880
When I got the call from Kameari Hospital,
I couldn't believe it.

211
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:43,600
We examined your body from top to bottom.

212
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,160
And we uncovered an astonishing fact.

213
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:48,020
What?

214
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:51,580
Are you saying there's
something wrong with my body?

215
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:53,480
That would be a problem!

216
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:56,160
All-you-can-eat yakiniku is waiting for me after this,
you know.

217
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:59,280
Now we'll move on to more specific tests.

218
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:01,080
Now, the first test.

219
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:01,800
Hup!

220
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:09,640
Eh?

221
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,440
Banana?

222
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:15,340
What is this?

223
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:18,980
Use those tongs and try
picking up the banana.

224
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:21,760
That's easy.

225
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:29,160
Mmmmm...

226
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:32,800
If I do it like this, I can grab it.

227
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,800
I got it so easily!

228
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,440
You were completely in series with it.

229
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,720
Functionality is high.

230
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,860
What can you possibly learn
from something like this?

231
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:43,940
Now, the next test.

232
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,620
Guess he can peel an apple, too.

233
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,680
I can do that much, you know!

234
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,660
There, is this what you want?

235
00:13:57,260 --> 00:14:00,220
The nurse is pretty useful.

236
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:01,540
Looks like today's the day!

237
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:02,360
Is this all it is?!

238
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,280
What on earth is this?

239
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:06,120
Now on to the next test.

240
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,540
Are we still doing this?!

241
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,940
Are you making a fool of me?!

242
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,620
How did it come to this?

243
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,140
There, finally.

244
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:17,200
What was it again? I can't recall.

245
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,600
Hey, listen.

246
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:22,160
Finally finished?

247
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,120
Fine, on to the next test.

248
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,260
Phew.

249
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:36,320
Aaaaaaaaah!

250
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:56,540
W-what is this?

251
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:56,740
This is...?

252
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:01,820
This is our laboratory's pride,
the realistic simulation system.

253
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:04,800
Now, for your next test,

254
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,358
that high ground rising up ahead,

255
00:15:07,408 --> 00:15:10,480
you are to go up and
fetch that torch over there.

256
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:16,000
What does something like this
have to do with a health checkup?

257
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:18,760
This is precisely the most important test!

258
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:21,040
Never mind that. What time is it now?

259
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:24,620
If you don't finish this quickly,
I won't be able to eat yakiniku!

260
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:27,080
How wonderful.

261
